You neglected to mention the scrolls you have already discovered, but
I will assume since you are only fourth level that you haven't
discovered many.  This is very important, since you can only write
scrolls you have already discovered in some form.  Actually, you *can*
try to write scrolls you haven't discovered yet, but unless you're
playing a Wizard you have only a 1/15 chance of success.

My advice would be to bless your magic marker (blessed mm's make
blessed scrolls), write a scroll of charging (to recharge the mm when
it starts running low), then scribble off a few scrolls of enchant
armor and enchant weapon.  I wouldn't waste my energy writing scrolls
of genocide since they require large amounts of energy and, imho, the
only monsters worth genociding are rust monsters and gelatinous cubes.
All the others can be handled easily given the proper equipment.

Remember, don't try to write a scroll your character hasn't identified
unless you *really* need it, and don't be too surprised when you fail.

